course: dictionary
lesson: 2250
title: How a crankshaft turns movement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A crankshaft is a long metal rod inside an engine. Its job is to change one kind of movement into another. The pistons move up and down, and the crankshaft turns that movement into spinning, which drives the wheels.
explain: «In a petrol or diesel engine, fuel burns in small cylinders and pushes pistons, which turn a crankshaft and then the wheels.» The sentence shows the order: pistons push, the crankshaft spins, and then the wheels turn.
explain: You can see the same idea on a bicycle. When you push the pedals up and down, the crank turns them round and round. Knowing one example helps you understand the other.
fact: A crankshaft is a long metal rod in an engine.
fact: A crankshaft changes up-and-down movement into turning (spinning) movement.
fact: «Pistons» are parts that move up and down inside an engine's cylinders.
fact: Cars, motorbikes, boats and old steam engines use crankshafts.
fact: A bicycle's pedals and crank work in a similar way, changing your leg movement into turning movement.
exercise: What does a crankshaft do? | *It changes up-and-down movement into turning movement | It stores petrol for the engine | It cools the wheels down | It makes the engine louder
exercise: «In a petrol or diesel engine, fuel burns in small cylinders and pushes pistons, which turn a crankshaft.» What pushes the crankshaft round? | The petrol tank | *The pistons | The driver's seat | The wheels
exercise: Which everyday object uses the same idea as a crankshaft? | A light switch | A drinking glass | *A bicycle's pedals and crank | A pair of socks
test: In a car engine, what does the crankshaft turn? | Wheels into the road | Spinning movement into a light that glows | Hot air into cold water | *Up-and-down movement into spinning movement that drives the wheels
test: Which of these uses crankshafts? | *An old steam engine | A paper clip | A pencil | A pair of scissors
exam: What is a crankshaft? | *A long metal rod that turns up-and-down movement into spinning movement | A small plastic bag for fuel | A tool for cutting metal | A type of wheel with no engine
